        <body>
            <div xml:id="d325">

                <pb facs="d324-02" n="2" sameAs="frus:frus1969-76ve05p1/d324-02"/>

                <head>325. Telegram 6540 From the Department of State to the Embassy in
                        Ethiopia<anchor n="1" xml:id="d325-f1"/>
                    <anchor n="2" xml:id="d325-f2"/>
                </head>
                <dateline><placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                        when="1972-01-12T00:54:00+00:00">January 12, 1972, 0054Z</date>
                </dateline>
                <pb facs="d325-01" n="1" xml:id="d325-01"/>
                <p>JOINT STATE/DEFENSE MESSAGE</p>
                <list subtype="subject" type="description">
                    <label>SUBJECT:</label>
                    <item>Kagnew STATION</item>
                </list>
                <list subtype="subject" type="description">
                    <label>REF:</label>
                    <item>State 3084; Addis 60 (NOTAL)</item>
                </list>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>As foreseen in State reftel, budgetary reductions for [<hi
                            rendition="#italic">text not declassified</hi>] make it necessary to
                        plan to close Kagnew [<hi rendition="#italic">text not declassified</hi>]
                        activity by end FY 72.</item>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>For planning, phase-down of [<hi rendition="#italic">text not
                            declassified</hi>] will begin within next few weeks with termination of
                            [<hi rendition="#italic">text not declassified</hi>] NLT 31 Mar. 72.
                        Site survey to identify economically recoverable [<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >text not declassified</hi>] equipment assets will be conducted as soon
                        as appropriate. Schedule for redeployment of personnel and release of
                        indigenous <pb facs="d325-02" n="2" xml:id="d325-02"/> personnel will be
                        established as soon as planning data can be obtained and implemented after
                        appropriate scenario for informing IEG worked out in collaboration with
                        Embassy.</item>
                    <label>3.</label>
                    <item>Interagency working group currently attempting to identify impact above
                        action will have on remaining functions (NAVCOMSTA, STRATCOM, [<hi
                            rendition="#italic">text not declassified</hi>], etc.), including [<hi
                            rendition="#italic">text not declassified</hi>] support activities, e.g.
                        hospital, commissary, R&amp;R facilities, etc.</item>
                    <label>4.</label>
                    <item>Appreciate problems this will pose for Country Team, but unforeseen
                        budgetary constraints have caused world-wide reductions in [<hi
                            rendition="#italic">text not declassified</hi>]. We wish to consult as
                        closely as possible with the CT on best manner to limit unfavorable
                        repercussions from reductions. One theme might be to describe reductions as
                        continuing process of cut-back made possible by technological advances and
                        for which IEG has earlier expressed approval, as suggested Addis 60.</item>
                    <pb facs="d325-03" n="3" xml:id="d325-03"/>
                    <label>5.</label>
                    <item>We would therefore appreciate CT assessment of expected IEG reaction,
                        impact on Asmara area including insurgency situation, and on USG-IEG
                        relations, as well asʼ suggested scenario for informing IEG. Since rumor of
                        impending phase-down already rife in Asmara, early reply
                        appreciated.<lb/>END</item>
                </list>
                <closer>
                    <signed> Rogers </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d325-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d325-f1-content">
                <p>Source: National Archives, RG 59, Central Files 1970–73, DEF 15–10 ETH–US.
                    Secret; Limdis; Priority. Drafted by Bader and Melone (AF/E); cleared in AF/E,
                    AF/RA, A/OC, PM/ISO, INR/DD, OASD/ISA, JCS; and approved by Newsom. Repeated to
                    JCS, USCINCEUR, Asmara, Addis Ababa, COMIDEASTFOR, and DIA.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d325-f2" n="2" xml:id="d325-f2-content">
                <p>This joint Department of State-Department of Defense telegram confirmed that
                    Kagnew would begin to phase-down its activities. The Country Team was asked to
                    forward its assessment of the Ethiopian Government reaction.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
